  data: {
    LLM: 'Non-dealer leads first trick. For each trick, second player follows suit if possible in standard form. Higher card of led suit wins unless a trump is played to a non-trump lead. In stage one, trick winner takes the exposed stock card and trick loser takes next hidden stock card; winner then leads next trick. After 13 tricks, stock is empty and stage two begins with no replenishment. Play 13 final tricks; these determine winner in standard scoring.',
    Player: 'Non-dealer leads first trick. For each trick, second player follows suit if possible in standard form. Higher card of led suit wins unless a trump is played to a non-trump lead. In stage one, trick winner takes the exposed stock card and trick loser takes next hidden stock card; winner then leads next trick. After 13 tricks, stock is empty and stage two begins with no replenishment. Play 13 final tricks; these determine winner in standard scoring.',
    objective: 'Win the majority of the 13 tricks in stage two after stock is exhausted.',
    gameplay: 'Non-dealer leads first trick. For each trick, second player follows suit if possible in standard form. Higher card of led suit wins unless a trump is played to a non-trump lead. In stage one, trick winner takes the exposed stock card and trick loser takes next hidden stock card; winner then leads next trick. After 13 tricks, stock is empty and stage two begins with no replenishment. Play 13 final tricks; these determine winner in standard scoring.',
    keyRules: [
      'Trump suit is fixed by the initial face-up stock card and does not change.',
      'Stage one tricks are for hand improvement, not usually for scoring the hand outcome.',
      'Stage two is a normal closed-hand trick contest with 13 tricks.',
      'Variant tables may count all 26 tricks or relax follow-suit in stage one.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
